  "claim": "Type `01 61`'s mode byte picks a length, and the five it picks stand in the ratio 3 : 4 : 6 : 8 : 12 -- the ratio the single pitch shifter's five windows were measured to stand in. Read as the distance the output holds a copy of itself at, with the shifter two semitones up where four takes of one state land 0.021 ms apart, the five states give 28.505, 38.000, 57.000, 75.995 and 114.026 ms -- against the first state 1.000, 1.333, 2.000, 2.666 and 4.000 where the ratio predicts 1, 1.333, 2, 2.667 and 4, every one of them inside that 0.021. At unison the same five land up to 10.52 ms apart from themselves, five hundred times further, so the reading the ratio rests on is the shifted one and the unison takes bound nothing. Each distance is 0.8906 of the window at the same state, to four figures across all five, and that multiple is not explained here.",
  "named": null,
  "adds": "This type carried no structural reading. It prints one shifter where the type beside it prints two and it prints a feedback byte that one does not, and the only claims naming it were the two that run across every type. What the window claim found was read off an artefact rate on one type; this is a distance in milliseconds on another, taken with a different stage, and it was predicted before the takes were made rather than read out of them.",
